//! ISA opcode tables of the PS5 shader translator: the PS5 source ISA (gfx1013) and the
//! AMD target ISAs it is translated to (gfx10.3, gfx11, gfx11.5, gfx12).
//!
//! Generated by `driver/tools/isa-tables/gen_isa_tables.py`; do not edit by hand.
//! Regenerate from the AnyPS5 checkout root with (add `--check` to verify that the
//! checked-in files are current):
//!
//! ```text
//! python driver\tools\isa-tables\gen_isa_tables.py `
//!     --llvm-build D:\projects\apple-llvm-project\.build-amdgpu `
//!     --llvm-src D:\projects\apple-llvm-project `
//!     --xml-zip C:\Users\Station\Documents\Codex\amd-isa-spec\mr_isa_latest.zip `
//!     --out driver\shader\src\ir\isa_gen
//! ```
//!
//! Sources:
//! - LLVM commit `3c1efa15830c5c60dbc45a3d3d47a1cacf5aba57`, TableGen output
//!   `AMDGPUGenMCCodeEmitter.inc` (fixed encoding bits), `AMDGPUGenAsmMatcher.inc` (mnemonics,
//!   real records and assembler predicates), `AMDGPUGenSubtargetInfo.inc` (CPU features),
//!   `AMDGPUGenInstrInfo.inc` (real record to pseudo mapping). [`OPERAND_SWAPS`] is derived
//!   from `llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/DSInstructions.td` and cross-checked against the selection
//!   patterns in `AMDGPUGenDAGISel.inc`.
//! - AMD machine-readable ISA XML bundle `AMD_GPU_MR_ISA_XML_2026_08_06.zip`, SHA-256
//!   `82404F1126761B7877595B622AFA7E1F311F2F41E89A3ABE9AAF8AD045C082E2`.
//!
//! Modules (LLVM CPU model, AMD XML architecture):
//! - [`ps5`]: `gfx1013`, `rdna2`, with
//!   `-mattr=+dot1-insts,+dot2-insts,+dot5-insts,+dot6-insts,+dot7-insts,+dot10-insts`.
//! - [`gfx1030`]: `gfx1030`, `rdna2`.
//! - [`gfx1100`]: `gfx1100`, `rdna3`.
//! - [`gfx1151`]: `gfx1151`, `rdna3_5`.
//! - [`gfx1200`]: `gfx1200`, `rdna4`.
//!
//! LLVM decides which opcodes exist: an opcode is listed when the LLVM assembler accepts one
//! of its real records on the CPU in wave32 or wave64 mode (and with or without
//! `real-true16` on CPUs with true16 instructions). AMD XML names are attached by
//! (encoding, opcode); opcodes that only the XML lists are in each module's `XML_ONLY`.
//!
